Z||000000||hugh||05-19-2001||09:53 AM||||Closed the shop early yesterday and went to the drags.I go to the national events at Englishtown and Maple Grove every year.If any of you get the chance to go to a national event,GO.There is nothing like seeing,hearing,and feeling 12,000 horsepower leave the starting line and powering a 2150 lb.car to 325MPH in just over 4.5 seconds.They shake the ground so much they set of car alarms with motion detectors in the parking lot.How about a car lifting the wheels so high you can see the whole frame,or a motorcycle carring the front wheel off the ground about 2 inches for the first 150 feet and running 185MPH in 7.2 seconds.I know there are a lot of folks on this forum that race now or have in the past.They have probably seen these cars and cycles.Those of you who haven't seen these vehicles have to do it to make their experiences in the auto world complete. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe4x4||05-19-2001||01:12 PM||||The need for speed......I was up to 172mph <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR>(Philly)<BR>No not the Fiero <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .....my street bike<BR>CBR 900 RR.<P>When I raced my bike down the track at Atco<BR>it was a RUSH. The 2nd time at the lights <BR>the front end came up and stayed up 1/2<BR>way down the track, first second third gear.<P>Hey Hugh ,<BR>maybe we should have a NJ Fiero meeting <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Local..I`ve been thinking about this .<BR>What do you think?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||1
